{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do","id":1402484,"title":"What Would Your God Do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-12T15:37:45-07:00","id":1402484,"title":"What Would Your God Do?","content":"Hello, I'm looking for sub-plot ideas for my campaign.<br /> <br /> The deity in question is a god of a local strip mine, one of two important features of a southern town (the other being an important crossroad of caravan routes.)<br /> The mine makes it a strategic location for the Realm, and is a stable job, making him important enough for the locals that they don't really have a separate god for the town itself.<br /> <br /> The problem is, the mine is getting depleted, and nobody among the other gods care. So, our god needs to either do something to extend its usefulness (get some extra resources assigned to it by the offices?), or get a new form of sustenance (somehow becoming important enough for the locals that he becomes the city god after the mine is no more) Problem is, he is a big fish in a small pond, important locally, but not really connected in Yu Shan or anything, and not super smart either.<br /> <br /> What I need for him is some sort of schemes he'd try to rope the player into in the effort to save himself, preferrably flawed ones, so he is forced to go through several through the campaign (possibly culminating in making some shady deal with Abyssals after everythging else fails)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T23:23:36-07:00","id":1402526,"title":"","content":"The first that comes to mind would be trying something like making it a sanctuary or a storage for other things. Maybe try to get mine remade into a sort of city or whatever, so he can become a city god via already being there. Attempt to strike an alliance with an elemental court that would make him a liaison and his mine a meeting spot that needs to be maintained or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T01:21:08-07:00","id":1402539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1402526#post1402526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first that comes to mind would be trying something like making it a sanctuary or a storage for other things. Maybe try to get mine remade into a sort of city or whatever, so he can become a city god via already being there. Attempt to strike an alliance with an elemental court that would make him a liaison and his mine a meeting spot that needs to be maintained or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's some start, although a bit more reasonable than I need... Please educate me on what an elemental court actually does. I mean, I've heard of them, but have always seen them as a bunch of disgruntled fire dudes sitting in a cave. What is their actual political influence and how do they do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T05:36:42-07:00","id":1402578,"title":"","content":"If the town is important to the Realm, your god could make clumsy overtures to the Immaculate Order. If they ordain him as the city god and give him a place on the calendar, then that's his problems solved!<br /> <br /> Only... they're not. Because Yu Shan could turn around at any minute and officially assign a different god. Or the town could be taken over by the Abyssals who end Immaculate Worship in favour of ancestor worship.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the social faux pas that this god would undoubtedly make when contacting the Immaculates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T06:29:41-07:00","id":1402589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1402578#post1402578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the town is important to the Realm, your god could make clumsy overtures to the Immaculate Order. If they ordain him as the city god and give him a place on the calendar, then that's his problems solved!<br /> <br /> Only... they're not. Because Yu Shan could turn around at any minute and officially assign a different god. Or the town could be taken over by the Abyssals who end Immaculate Worship in favour of ancestor worship.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the social faux pas that this god would undoubtedly make when contacting the Immaculates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now we're getting somewhere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And where could we fit the solar here? She lives in town, working as a doctor, and hiding her powers so far (because revealing herself would leave her on the run, and force her to abandon her patients. She's a bit of a sociopath, but doesn't feel like conquering stuff. Also, she prefers the Realm here, seeing them as a stable option, for all their flaws - because the local resistance has made a very bad impression on her, as it is sponsored by the abyssals) Her secret is the god's leverage on her, though he hasn't been calous enough to push it yet - he actually wants her on his side. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T07:25:24-07:00","id":1402595,"title":"","content":"There's a few avenues here.<br /> <br /> Solar vs Realm. The god wants Immaculate backing. The Immaculates want a tighter hold on the town. The Solar wants Realm stability... but does want a Wyld Hunt. Left alone... the god is going to put the town firmly under heel. Does the Solar now have to reevaluate her support of the Realm? Does she directly intercede to make sure the god gets what he wants but the town doesn't suffer? Does she keep her head down as her hometown turns into some kind of Orwellian nightmare?<br /> <br /> There's Solar for God. I'm assuming your Lawbringer is a Twilight, not an Eclipse diplomat or Zenith priest? As a Twilight the realm of spirits sits within her purview. Maybe your god enlists her to do the negotiating with the Immaculates on his behalf? After all, the Immaculates don't know she's a Solar, but she's bound to be more competent (in the god's mind) than a mortal (this could be a gross miscalculation).<br /> <br /> There's Solar vs God. The Immaculate Philosophy has pretty strict rules about gods not interacting with mortals. How does a god, then, parlay with the Immaculates? Does he manifest, breaking faith, and speak for himself? Does he converse with his priests, breaking faith, and send them to speak on his behalf? There's plenty of room for misunderstandings and wilful interpretation here. How does your Solar feel about treating the broken legs of the mortal sent to go negotiate with Peleps Delad? Or about this god clumsily bargaining with the Dragon-Blooded when he knows her secret?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T05:38:42-07:00","id":1402788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1402539#post1402539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's some start, although a bit more reasonable than I need... Please educate me on what an elemental court actually does. I mean, I've heard of them, but have always seen them as a bunch of disgruntled fire dudes sitting in a cave. What is their actual political influence and how do they do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>-An elemental court is simpler than a divine court. Use a tribal system. They are usually reactive to problems caused by other elementals, Out of Fate beings or irresponsible deities.<br /> <br /> -Work in Bureaus of Seasons (mainly) and Nature. They monitor living beings, material components and/or natural phenomena in a region. A court linked to the Bureaus of Seasons is usually a military reserve force (useful charms for mass destruction).<br /> <br /> -A Cselenine pact (payment in Jade) or worship can convince an elemental court to include other matters as their function. The nature of the majority determines the policy of court, Wood elementals are meritocrats, Earth elementals do not tolerate Shadowlands and Wyld, Fire elementals defend marriages or duels, Water elementals participate in rebellions and Air elementals accept complex systems of organization..<br /> <br /> NOTE: Sorry for my mistakes. English is not my native language","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T07:37:40-07:00","id":1402805,"title":"","content":"The Council of Winds is the most powerful elemental court in Creation. They control each court in the north and west. Its headquarters are on Mount Meru. They secretly hunt Water elementals for 1000 years (Yu-Shan ignores crimes in exchange for cooperation). Its role is to oversee the climate for the Bureau of Seasons.<br /> <br /> The Orderly Flame is the biggest court. There are no members on the Blessed Island. Its headquarters is in the south. Its function is to promote the good image of the fire element, in honor of the disappeared censor Swan Dragon.<br /> <br /> The most common is Mineral and the Mountains. The large number of them and many members do not guarantee influence because they are recluse. They inspect the soil components of Creation and hunt down hostile darkbroods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T11:03:30-07:00","id":1402836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rochedo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1402805#post1402805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Council of Winds is the most powerful elemental court in Creation. They control each court in the north and west. Its headquarters are on Mount Meru. They secretly hunt Water elementals for 1000 years (Yu-Shan ignores crimes in exchange for cooperation). Its role is to oversee the climate for the Bureau of Seasons.<br /> <br /> The Orderly Flame is the biggest court. There are no members on the Blessed Island. Its headquarters is in the south. Its function is to promote the good image of the fire element, in honor of the disappeared censor Swan Dragon.<br /> <br /> The most common is Mineral and the Mountains. The large number of them and many members do not guarantee influence because they are recluse. They inspect the soil components of Creation and hunt down hostile darkbroods.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I go the Elemental Courts route, it would be fire - both because the adventure is set in the south, and the strip mine contains fire dust (back when I started the campaign I wasn't quite clear on some details of lore) So what can they do for him and what could he do for them? Do they have their own people in the ministries, or do they just sit in Creation and do their own thing while ignoring Yu Shan's will?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T11:10:27-07:00","id":1402966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do#post1402484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">get a new form of sustenance</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to clarify that gods in Exalted don't need prayer for sustenance; they find it pleasurable and satisfying, but they don't wither and die without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T12:08:04-07:00","id":1402973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1402539#post1402539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please educate me on what an elemental court actually does. I mean, I've heard of them, but have always seen them as a bunch of disgruntled fire dudes sitting in a cave. What is their actual political influence and how do they do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic format of a spirit court is that it's how spirits form into a local hierarchy and socialise. The main thing of them is establishing an order of precedent so that spirits can co-exist without stepping on each other's toes in terms of their worldly purviews and any worshippers they might accumulate (even if they likely scheme amongst one another to extend their power within protocol). It also lets them form a collective of protection against other spirits that might muscle in on their territory. They can tend to form around a spirit who either has the strength to offer that protection and keep everybody under the umbrella playing nice, or is respectable, charismatic or well-organized enough to be a stabilizing influence whose interventions are agreeable to all.<br /> <br /> Courts have significance in a world where the Terrestrial gods are often ruthless and the authority of Heaven is limited and disinterested.<br /> <br /> You do have a few more specialized courts with more abstract mission statements. The Court of Orderly Flame is an organisation of Southern elementals (mostly fire) dedicated to the memory of an exceptionally upright and honourable dragon Censor who was lost to the Fair Folk invasion. They try to incentivize other spirits to live up to those high standards and promote decency and justice. The Court of Seasons is simply the collective of the gods who represent each calendar month, although they're also charged with the responsibility of managing the Carnival of Meetings, the grand festival that takes place in Yu-Shan each Calibration. This gives them a popularity out of proportion with what they actually do, and they're pretty big-headed over it. <br /> <br /> Previous Editions have written Yu-Shan as considering disbanding the Bureau of Seasons (which governs Creation's weather and climate) and giving those responsibilities to the Court of Seasons, unaware that they are woefully unqualified.<br /> <br /> The funny thing to me is that while the game uses the term 'court', evocative of the attendants of monarchs and powerful aristocrats, they're a lot more reminiscent of the ancient Roman concept of the collegium.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T14:14:59-07:00","id":1402983,"title":"","content":"If OP is looking for plothooks centering on the god trying to keep his job, then I can think of several things. These two ideas can both be applied, one as a starter adventure, the next one as the big main campaign.<br /> <br /> 1) Recruit the players to strong-arm local earth elementals into submitting to him. Basically have the players become the god's leg-breakers as he builds his own elemental court up.<br /> - this will of course lead to future conflict with local elemental courts, but that's just more leg-breaking<br /> - that will in turn lead to conflict with sidereals as this god suddenly starts wielding a lot more power than he was meant to have. Not sure you can leg-break your way out of this one, perhaps try some heavenly diplomacy?<br /> <br /> 2) In the gods search for ways to make the mine a more permanent location of interest, he asks around and learns of the legend of the Drop That Contained A Sea, a first age artifact used to instantly conjure up vast amounts of water. He wants to turn his strip mine into an oasis, capitalizing on the traffic that comes via the trade road. A massive water supply would draw in caravans from all over, making him far more powerful, especially if he can be sure that the locals are thanking him for the water<br /> - This means getting the players to quest for this ancient and lost artifact<br /> - It was used by the solars back in the first age, but... apparently hasn't been used since - so where'd it go?<br /> - the players can ask around and learn that it was last used to create the lakes and waterways that define the Harborhead territories, back in the late first age, about four hundred or so years before the great contagion. It was of course lost after that.<br /> - poking around black market artifact auctions in Chiaroscuro, the players learn that in the immideate years after the great contagion, when her Redness took power and formalized the immaculate monks, a lot of first age artifacts that had previously been used by the DBs in the late first age were hidden away because they bore too many marks of their Solar origins.<br /> - so... find the hidden artifact?<br /> - the central administration for the immaculates in the south is in the Lap, via a monestary located behind the central grand immaculate temple in the city. It's administrative library contains the ledgers that detail what was hidden where. Good luck finding that ledger, because book-keeping from 700 years ago on hidden artifacts is very frail and very secret.<br /> - once they find the ledger, crack the code and find the location, its off the temple where the drop is hidden.<br /> - the temple turns out to be a very remote monestary for asshole DB monks in the south that nobody else really wants around. So they're all assholes.<br /> - the drop is locked away in a magical vault manse under the monestary. The password is a special prayer known only to the abbot of the monestary... or, abbots, because up until recently it was run by two DB brothers.<br /> - problem is that one brother wanted to be less of an asshole and left the place, so even if the players can talk the remaining abbot into telling them his half of the prayer, they need to find the other guy<br /> - The lost brother travelled to the east<br /> - got captured by Lookshy<br /> - commited suicide, to prevent the secret prayer-password from falling into non-realm hands<br /> - shit<br /> - except... the abbot(s) apparently undergo a ritual when they learn the prayer, marking their souls. It makes them guaranteed to return as ghosts, to prevent the prayer passwords from being lost forever if they die without teaching someone else the prayer. But the ghost is nowhere to be seen.<br /> - and where to ghosts of people who commit suicide while in prison go? the players will have to ask around<br /> - time for an adventure into the Eternal Prison in the labyrinth of the underworld (see Compass: Underworld p 122) <br /> - if the players can bust in, find the ghost of the DB, get the info, and get out again, then... the strip mine god gets his oasis and throws a nice beach party for the players","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T07:38:02-07:00","id":1403098,"title":"","content":"Excuse me. The Orderly Flame is the most powerful elemental court. It is a fire court syndicate.<br /> The Council of Winds is the highest elemental court (declares all air elementals as members).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1402836#post1402836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I go the Elemental Courts route, it would be fire - both because the adventure is set in the south, and the strip mine contains fire dust (back when I started the campaign I wasn't quite clear on some details of lore) So what can they do for him and what could he do for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deities are organized in a bureaucracy. They report and make decisions based on objectives created by Yu-Shan. I don't know how they do the reports, I believe they are prayers. A deity can be biased, silent or acquire a debt. The court can provide a background to divinity projects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they have their own people in the ministries, or do they just sit in Creation and do their own thing while ignoring Yu Shan's will? </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Usually an elemental court exists because the divine court has failed. Several deities abandoned Creation during the Crusade. Yu-Shan discovered that the elementals voluntarily occupied this space and preferred to continue (but it generated several unemployed deities).<br /> The Orderly Flame wants power in the celestial bureaucracy to remain autonomous. They obey Yu-Shan if they respect the principles of Swan Dragon. For the same reason there is tension with the Guild and The Realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2150-rochedo","name":"Rochedo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T12:07:28-07:00","id":1403139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1402983#post1402983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If OP is looking for plothooks centering on the god trying to keep his job, then I can think of several things. These two ideas can both be applied, one as a starter adventure, the next one as the big main campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Key element - it is a single player campaign with a medicine supernal twilight whose theme is 'town medic trying and failing to keep a low profile.' She wouldn't break anyone's legs except to set them properly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> She has only started learning just how much she can do with just first circle sorcery, and her current biggest ambition is to get the local merchants to sponsor a proper hospital in town.<br /> <br /> There is a gold faction sidereal in town, trying to manipulate her into becoming a hero, but he knows she wouldn't survive a wyld hunt if he forced to reveal herself early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T17:50:21-07:00","id":1403164,"title":"","content":"It bears considering that information about elementals in older Editions needs to be reconciled with the current one having completely dropped the idea that they originated after the Primordial War in an explicitly subordinate position to gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T01:07:00-07:00","id":1403349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1403139#post1403139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Key element - it is a single player campaign with a medicine supernal twilight whose theme is 'town medic trying and failing to keep a low profile.' She wouldn't break anyone's legs except to set them properly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> She has only started learning just how much she can do with just first circle sorcery, and her current biggest ambition is to get the local merchants to sponsor a proper hospital in town.<br /> <br /> There is a gold faction sidereal in town, trying to manipulate her into becoming a hero, but he knows she wouldn't survive a wyld hunt if he forced to reveal herself early.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A twilight has Investigation charms. that means truth-telling charms. that means being able to force the truth out of people, which means blackmail. plus, as a doctor he must have some social charms/skills, especially if playing solo<br /> <br /> and if its a healer, then the god can simply try to spin his request by saying that he needs the earth elemntals &quot;convinced&quot; to work for him- you can reword the leg breaker thing. that was more if you had a circle of players including a fighter, in case that player would want to wrestle an elemental into submission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T19:04:38-07:00","id":1403460,"title":"","content":"First things first: <br /> <br /> - What is mined in the place and how important is it to Realm or satrapy?<br /> - How deep in the South is It? How much of this wealth goes in essentials like importing food or water?<br /> - What have you defined of the deity, is It male, female, genderless, hermaphroditic, literally genderfluid changing according to whim or esoteric criteria? What kind of personality does It have? The fact it's covering for a solar, trying to also play city god AND making plans about actively avoiding a loss of worship makes me think he's too self-interested to be truly chummy with the Immaculates.<br /> - You cited &quot;an important crossroad of caravan routes&quot; also. Wouldn't that have a good too, one probably far more adequate to the role of city god AND assuring the city's continued fortune? I could see some serious rivalry brewing If they are not lovers or somesuch (and even then perhaps).<br /> <br /> Just some quick thoughts to help into fleshing out the scenario and maybe anchor your ideas. The more you give us, the more effective our suggestions can get. Hope It helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T02:27:05-07:00","id":1403503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1403349#post1403349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A twilight has Investigation charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Some</i> Twilights have Investigation Charms. In my experience, even in 1e and 2e where you being a Twilight Caste meant you had to have these five distinct Caste Abilities, that didn't mean you were going to use all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1403349#post1403349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that means truth-telling charms. that means being able to force the truth out of people...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue the overall theme of Solar Investigation is &quot;discovering and processing clues to produce answers.&quot; Judge's Ear Technique does not &quot;force the truth out of people&quot; - it just reveals their lie. Even Irresistible Questioning Technique, <i>one Charm</i> in the Solar investigator's arsenal, is fairly limited in its application.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1403349#post1403349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which means blackmail.</div> </div> </div> </div>The poster <i>said </i>the character is trying to keep a low profile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T08:30:26-07:00","id":1403528,"title":"","content":"As an aside, OP are you certain about the strip mine thing? Because from what i have seen all forms of surface-mining tend to be quite infrastructure-heavy even for pre-industrial settings, many requiring lots of WATER to wash off the overburden (undesired soil). What might be VERY counterproductive in a direction where potable water is usually at a premium.<br /> <br /> Not to mention It usually produces no tunnels, but one ginormous pit. Just wanted some clarification on that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T10:14:24-07:00","id":1403542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1403503#post1403503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Some</i> Twilights have Investigation Charms. In my experience, even in 1e and 2e where you being a Twilight Caste meant you had to have these five distinct Caste Abilities, that didn't mean you were going to use all of them.<br /> <br /> I'd argue the overall theme of Solar Investigation is &quot;discovering and processing clues to produce answers.&quot; Judge's Ear Technique does not &quot;force the truth out of people&quot; - it just reveals their lie. Even Irresistible Questioning Technique, <i>one Charm</i> in the Solar investigator's arsenal, is fairly limited in its application.<br /> <br /> The poster <i>said </i>the character is trying to keep a low profile.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> blackmail can be a perfectly doable way of staying low profile. Plus, its a twilight caste, not a night caste. They don't do low profile in the same way, but I guess it all depends on how you play it<br /> <br /> Either way, my suggestions still work just fine. If you're playing 2nd ed there's the charm that lets you know the heart's price - now that's a great way to figure out exactly how to make people cooperate with you and get things working smoothly. Or blackmail them - whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T13:57:03-07:00","id":1403565,"title":"","content":"I think the issue here is that the thread is aiming for ideas to expand the plots of one game, specially through agendas, motives and plots of a NPC - and you decided to push for PC behaviour, that one thing the ST has less control over and one that, while indeed perfectly viable for Twilights in general, might run somewhat counter to the style of said character from what little we got on its portrayal so far, as i believe Alucard meant to point out.<br /> <br /> I agree, both me and he could be incorrect in that impression so far, but even being the case, the ST is better off focusing on NPC projects than directing/predicting those of a PC, specially in a solo game, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T14:45:26-07:00","id":1404307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1403460#post1403460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First things first:<br /> <br /> - What is mined in the place and how important is it to Realm or satrapy?<br /> - How deep in the South is It? How much of this wealth goes in essentials like importing food or water?<br /> - What have you defined of the deity, is It male, female, genderless, hermaphroditic, literally genderfluid changing according to whim or esoteric criteria? What kind of personality does It have? The fact it's covering for a solar, trying to also play city god AND making plans about actively avoiding a loss of worship makes me think he's too self-interested to be truly chummy with the Immaculates.<br /> - You cited &quot;an important crossroad of caravan routes&quot; also. Wouldn't that have a good too, one probably far more adequate to the role of city god AND assuring the city's continued fortune? I could see some serious rivalry brewing If they are not lovers or somesuch (and even then perhaps).<br /> <br /> Just some quick thoughts to help into fleshing out the scenario and maybe anchor your ideas. The more you give us, the more effective our suggestions can get. Hope It helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok then...<br /> <br /> 1 I didn't know all the lore when I started the campaign (and really, every deviation from the norm in Exalted can be explained with 'an old solar did it' ) so the mine contains firedust, something that is usually combed from the desert much further south. The satrapy itself is rather small, and currently held by a single legion loyal to Ragara, one dragon here and one in the capital. That means the mine is key to the locals, and a strategic resource to Ragara. Other houses won't care if the mine is threatened, but will act if the city itself is under threat, because of its location on the road to Gem.<br /> <br /> 2 The place is located on the southern side of the mountain range, about a week south-west from the spot where the caravans from Chirascuro and Lap would meet on their way to Gem. They are close enough to the mountains (having a mine in the mountain side) that water is supplied by an aqueduct, enough for some locals to grow dates (but also making it a very important strategic weak spot someone could mess with)<br /> <br /> 3 the god is male. He shows up as a chubby black dude dressed in red silks and gold, styling himself as a benevolent host who brings generous gifts to the miners. (mostly it's just their hard work though.) He is strategic enough that he can show up and talk down to people despite the location (there are some immaculates there, but the closest powerful ones are in the capital - the only local dragonborn are the officers in the army) but he knows this might end soon, and he very uch doesn't want that. He might have little experience interacting with actual immaculate monks. <br /> <br /> 4 There are two kinds of people in town, those who work in the mine, and those who work as farmers and traders to supply the caravans. But while the mine is a specific place, trade and caravans are an activity, more likely to have some god in Yu Shan. Most of matters related to traffic are handled by minor gods presiding over the oases along the way. If there is a god of caravans directly in town, he hasn't shown up yet. (so, yes, there is space there for some ideas)<br /> <br /> 5 Yes, a huge hole in the ground. Logistical problems in Exalted are usually solved by throwing more slaves at them (only a fraction of miners are free locals). Also, if you're digging something that's potentially explosive, you really don't want to be in a tunnel. <br /> <br /> 6 Of other things:<br /> - ever since the Realm forces stopped getting reinforcements, there has been some local resistance movement. Sadly it is already infiltrated by servants of FAFL (mostly ghosts acting through possessed agents) trying to escalate the conflict into a sad bloodbath. They've already angered one of the oasis gods (and lots of merchants) by dropping their dead into an oasis pond.<br /> - the sidereal agent is posing as the garrison wizard to the dracon. He pretends to have seen 'potential for magic' in the PC and mentors her by roping her into quests connected to his magic, helping with weaving a spell to protect the mine warehouses from arson, sending her with some soldiers on ingredients hunts, etc. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T04:27:33-07:00","id":1404566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404307#post1404307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok then...<br /> <br /> 1 I didn't know all the lore when I started the campaign (and really, every deviation from the norm in Exalted can be explained with 'an old solar did it' ) so the mine contains firedust, something that is usually combed from the desert much further south. The satrapy itself is rather small, and currently held by a single legion loyal to Ragara, one dragon here and one in the capital. That means the mine is key to the locals, and a strategic resource to Ragara. Other houses won't care if the mine is threatened, but will act if the city itself is under threat, because of its location on the road to Gem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, so the satrapy is in House Ragara's hands, though at least one other house also has a presence in the capital - the mine being more of a venture of the Ragaras, while for the other house(s) what really matters is the trade caravans going all the way to Gem. Sabotaging things in the area might be a valid way to distract the satrap and his Ragara ilk of (in their opinion) more important intrigues going on in the capital.<br /> <br /> Since you spoke of two dragons, where are other 8 that compose the Ragara legion in the satrapy, wandering the nation in search of bandits/rebels to enslave, giving their somewhat green troops much needed shakedown and experience, setting up new roads and fortifications to cement the house's hold in the region, hunting for anathema or manse's for the commander's and its house (probably in that order) vainglory or something more obscure and weird?<br /> <br /> Speaking of lore, Firedust has been described in books as gathered from certain sands and made from peculiar forms of pollen <b>both</b>. Creation is not a world for standardized scientific nomenclature and data anyway, so it might be perfectly possible that what is called &quot;firedust&quot; covers a variety of materials, much like &quot;jade&quot; in the real world is two different minerals. No worries about that.<br /> <br /> Me, for ease of reference, try to take inspiration from wiki bits on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphorus#History\" target=\"_blank\">phosphorus</a> and how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphorus#Bone_ash_and_guano\" target=\"_blank\">bone ash &amp; guano</a> - read petrified bones and remains - can be important strategic sources of these. Maybe a natural byproduct of when the gaze of the Sun, the touch of Hesiesh (or their respective Chosen) eliminates great quantities of sapient or animal carcasses in any one place. Right there - with some <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_Valley\" target=\"_blank\">real life samples</a> - you got a nice hook for why ghosts and abyssals might be messing around such a mine. As an aside, though different in important ways (like city and mine apparently being one and same) Zoatham, on pages 98-100 of the corebook, might be worth looking into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404307#post1404307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 The place is located on the southern side of the mountain range, about a week south-west from the spot where the caravans from Chirascuro and Lap would meet on their way to Gem. They are close enough to the mountains (having a mine in the mountain side) that water is supplied by an aqueduct, enough for some locals to grow dates (but also making it a very important strategic weak spot someone could mess with)</div> </div> </div> </div>Must admit the Chiaroscuro reference, being much more easterly than the Lap or Gem, more confuses than helps with imagining where it might be on the map, but for ease of visuals i'm thinking &quot;somewhere in the ginormous southwestern mountain range hugging An-Teng, Goldenseal &amp; etc&quot;, possible places for merchants, spies &amp; all kinds of adventurers or troublemakers to come from. More directly important, local sources of food &amp; water exist, so the place is <i><b>not</b></i> completely dependent on caravans &amp; exports - partly explaining why caravan/commerce deities are not even pushier than the mine god - but that might also make for a potential point of dispute, as water &amp; food that goes to the mine is more of the local bounty that is being &quot;stolen&quot; from the natives. Wells, minor rivers and oases might be kept secret by some local families to help maintain their agriculture, sought by those with dreams of sudden wealth and influence the interactions of natives and foreigners with any spirits (specially those related to fertility, water &amp; wood), among other things.<br /> <br /> Incidentally <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphate#Geological_occurrence\" target=\"_blank\">Morocco</a> is a major global exporter of phosphorus and dates, so it might be a good place to look into for extra imagery/ideas if you're in the mood for some reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404307#post1404307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 the god is male. He shows up as a chubby black dude dressed in red silks and gold, styling himself as a benevolent host who brings generous gifts to the miners. (mostly it's just their hard work though.) He is strategic enough that he can show up and talk down to people despite the location (there are some immaculates there, but the closest powerful ones are in the capital - the only local dragonborn are the officers in the army) but he knows this might end soon, and he very much doesn't want that. He might have little experience interacting with actual immaculate monks.<br /> <br /> 4 There are two kinds of people in town, those who work in the mine, and those who work as farmers and traders to supply the caravans. But while the mine is a specific place, trade and caravans are an activity, more likely to have some god in Yu Shan. Most of matters related to traffic are handled by minor gods presiding over the oases along the way. If there is a god of caravans directly in town, he hasn't shown up yet. (so, yes, there is space there for some ideas).</div> </div> </div> </div>He has a peculiar situation indeed. His purview makes him something like a Field Guardian, though with far more wealth but, unfortunately for him, a finite non-renewable one (unless he starts gathering a huge pile of animal and human carcasses, guano, excrements &amp; other remains somewhere). His job has a definite deadline and the sands of time are trickling against him - if he doesn't watch out he might end up without a job, or if he's lucky enough to have a (currently) secondary, older role as god of a specific mountain, the patch of land the mining pit is located upon or something along those lines, not unemployed, but with a much reduced purview, influence and wealth. What could be even worse depending on his ego or how many enemies he made in the process of becoming what he presently is.<br /> <br /> But back on basics, does he have priests, formal or informal ones? Lovers, one or multiple, mortal, spirit, exalted, exigent or other? Does he have a gender preference or appreciates both males &amp; females? Are any of those relationships solids or mayfly romances that come and go?<br /> <br /> (Damn, just crossed my mind the creepy image of him keeping a mortal espouse/lover <b><i>after </i></b>death as a ghost, hungry ghost, animated - or all of those, for that extra WTF factor - or, at least changing them into something partly elemental upon demise)<br /> <br /> Does he have god-blooded childer, human, animal or beastman?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404307#post1404307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 Yes, a huge hole in the ground. Logistical problems in Exalted are usually solved by throwing more slaves at them (only a fraction of miners are free locals). Also, if you're digging something that's potentially explosive, you really don't want to be in a tunnel.</div> </div> </div> </div>What in itself adds some fun complications - on one side you have a bunch of slaves on a particularly hazardous &amp; miserable enviroment that has a great potential for producing small shadowlands here and there from lost dead miners and contact with ghosts &amp; other Underworld entities (even without bringing into the mix the posible phosphorus/carcasses associations i previously pointed out).<br /> <br /> On another, it means that the greater part of the native population has <b>no </b>access or involvment with - and consequently, gets little to no benefit from - <b><i>the largest source of wealth in the area</i></b>, what is sure to engender some resentment from the lower classes toward those who actually benefit directly from it (as overseers, managers, guards, slave providers &amp; so on), along with the exploitative Realm foreigners that enable them. Well, except for those natives who get turned in slaves as punishment for crimes (real or fabricated for the sake of covering personnel quotas, petty revenge or more) or payment of family debts. But those are incidents that bring whole new brands of outrage &amp; resentement (exploitable by the forces of the dead) to the mix, i bet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404307#post1404307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6 Of other things:<br /> - ever since the Realm forces stopped getting reinforcements, there has been some local resistance movement. Sadly it is already infiltrated by servants of FAFL (mostly ghosts acting through possessed agents) trying to escalate the conflict into a sad bloodbath. They've already angered one of the oasis gods (and lots of merchants) by dropping their dead into an oasis pond.<br /> - the sidereal agent is posing as the garrison wizard to the dracon. He pretends to have seen 'potential for magic' in the PC and mentors her by roping her into quests connected to his magic, helping with weaving a spell to protect the mine warehouses from arson, sending her with some soldiers on ingredients hunts, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe capturing the hungry ghosts of dead slaves or assassinate guards &amp; overseers for use as supernatural attack hounds against Ragara troops and other adversaries in the city or other regions? And the god is unhappy because he feels those particular undead are <b>his </b>to use or dispose of according to his interests, esoteric or self-serving?<br /> <br /> So, the sidereal is playing double agent, serving a dynast while actually using the position for sabotage - or at least advance his own agenda. Well, supposing the garrison commander is opposed to making deals with Anathema. Considering it is a Ragara we are speaking of, could be the complete opposite of fact. Damn, the dragon-blooded could even be setting up some sort of shell game with the Abyssal, creating a revolution scenario that actually serves for them to cut ties to their respective masters and strike as overlords on their own.<br /> <br /> Decided to explore that &quot;i was a god of this place before there was a city or mine&quot; angle i commented, resulting some peculiar images coming up that get the bits about &quot;firedust/phosphorus from ashes of dead/unclean things&quot;, ideas about its interactions with worshippers mine workers and slaves both among others and pull all of them together in a distinct whole. The end result is probably not quite what you had in mind - in fact, i suspect i might have made something far older and sinister hiding behind the &quot;noveau rich god&quot; veneer, like a <i>gh\u00fcl </i>prettified with a belly-dancer's veils - but it's looking quite promising i think, so bear with me.<br /> <br /> He's a god of wealth, of hidden (secret) treasures covered by earth, but also a scary, threatening deity, he who knows all its paths &amp; pitfalls, where the careless, disrespectful or ungrateful may get lost, hurt, fall to their doom or find itself broken and buried by a landslide. A god who knows where the skeletons, metaphorical and literal, are hidden and decides what stays buried and what unclean thing is dragged to dry under the sun's unblinking gaze.<br /> <br /> Before there was firedust to be harvested, through the ages a quicksand pit existed, guarding that stretch of the mountains, a place where countless multitudes of time forgotten beings - animal herds, trade caravans, migratory bands, overconfident armies - would be dragged to places below to die and fester. He keeps their wealth, their remains, sometimes their names and memories. The Lord of the Pit he is, much like he was long before a city and a mine formed around him, with mortals praying for his beneficence and mercy. And if the wealth is ever played out - well, time to start harvesting again.<br /> <br /> Statwise, i would make this particular version by mixing up the QCs' of Field Guardian and Storm Mother (maybe some bit of Hound of Unbroken Earth, your choice), adjusting the charms according to the mine/sand pit theme with avalanches/burial in place of storms &amp; drowning, firedust for lightning and so on.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts. Definitely going to use this version in one of my games in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-25-2020, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T14:07:22-07:00","id":1404831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404566#post1404566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just some thoughts. Definitely going to use this version in one of my games in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've done a lot of research. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 1 I made a major brain derp. Somehow I was convinced that &quot;each rank is twice as many&quot; continues all the way up above a claw - and now I have to figure out where the other 8 dragons are...<br /> <br /> 2 I'm using old maps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There used to be mountains south of Lap that forced their caravans to Gem to go south west before they could go south east.<br /> <br /> 3 The god has only shown twice so far, so his family life hasn't been relevant yet. Certainly something to consider. As far as I thought until now, he used to be just the god of the mountain, but it wasn't really relevant until the deposit was discovered - you don't really pray to a mountain god unless you have a reason to climb it or unless it starts smoking (which very well might have been the case in ages past, southern mountains and all.)<br /> <br /> 4 He has a small shrine that the miners use. There is also a local temple that pays lip service to the immaculate philosophy but still employs local rituals for dealing with gods and spirits. There is a young but gifted priestess they send on errands when one needs to be placated.<br /> <br /> 5 So far the resistance has been targetting the mine to weaken the Realm influence - but a potential wealth that comes from it could be used as an incentive to get some nobles on their side. That's how revolutions are financed, whatever simple people would like to think. (Also, while mistreatment of slaves is obviously a thing, as are various horrors of Exalted, I don't want to make my campaign too dark. My player and I used to have a World of Darkness storyteller who used to overdo it, and the campaign crashed and burned from darkness-induced audience apathy.)<br /> <br /> 6 So, the resistance would stoop to grave-robbing to produce evil spirits that could be chained to their service? An interesting idea. How can a mortal enslave a hungry ghost without getting his throat torn out? <br /> <br /> 7 The sidereal is pushing his own agenda, but not really scheming against Ragara so far - if only because their presence there offers the city more stability than the current alternative. So he actually does help them foil the more sinister moves against them. As for the Dragon blooded, turning against the Realm hasn't crossed their minds just yet, although the younger ones definitely resent being stuck without support on what they consider a backwater. That also means they'd try to kill the PC if they discovered her now. <br /> <br /> 8 I don't think the quicksand quite fits, but he could definitely have a darker side. Even in real life mythology, mine gods and spirits are usually fickle, even if benevolent. After all, they also embody the OSHA rules of the mine - disrespecting those can get you killed really quickly. So far I'm imagining him as a kind of spoiled aristocrat stereotype - too vain and greedy to realise how dangerously stupid he is (kind of like the badger god in the old Sidereal book introductory comic. ) EDIT: I checked notes, and the mountain is a dead volcano. So your plan could work - although the god probably has no authority or enough power to make the mountain erupt again without some Yu Shan paperwork. Definitely a direction to explore in the future. <br /> <br /> If you want more details, here are my campaign notes so far (there is some captain obvious info there - it was meant for brainstorming with people unfamiliar with Exalted) <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Vots16qiWe9az3Gea8XjybufAf2tCEvjYrrWC5rODBk/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Vots16qiWe9az3Gea8XjybufAf2tCEvjYrrWC5rODBk/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Vots16qiWe9az3Gea8XjybufAf2tCEvjYrrWC5rODBk/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Vots16qiWe9az3Gea8XjybufAf2tCEvjYrrWC5rODBk/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T17:29:49-07:00","id":1405220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've done a lot of research. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Google and Wiki help so much always. Something of a compulsive reader/world-builder too, i guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And before i forget - again - what is the name of the city, the kingdom and capital?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 I made a major brain derp. Somehow I was convinced that &quot;each rank is twice as many&quot; continues all the way up above a claw - and now I have to figure out where the other 8 dragons are...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so you thought a dragon was half a legion! It happens, no prob. You can either stick to your &quot;legion in the kingdom is divided in two major groups&quot; initial idea and have each half (5 legions) in a place, or in a little act of misdirection, have one dragon in the city and the other 9 dragons of troops in the capital, as a way to convince the other DBs in the satrapy that the mine while relatively relevant, is still a minor priority to the Ragaras.<br /> <br /> Or maybe some of the desert tribes cited that are causing trouble to Gem deeper the South have moved in an attempt to block the flow of mercenary help and the other 8 dragons of Realm troops are dealing with that or something else like a Lunar or Raksha warlord, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 I'm using old maps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There used to be mountains south of Lap that forced their caravans to Gem to go south west before they could go south east.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could always try to play with the maps and editing one with elements of multiple editions according to your interests.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 The god has only shown twice so far, so his family life hasn't been relevant yet. Certainly something to consider. As far as I thought until now, he used to be just the god of the mountain, but it wasn't really relevant until the deposit was discovered - you don't really pray to a mountain god unless you have a reason to climb it or unless it starts smoking (which very well might have been the case in ages past, southern mountains and all.)<br /> <br /> 4 He has a small shrine that the miners use. There is also a local temple that pays lip service to the immaculate philosophy but still employs local rituals for dealing with gods and spirits. There is a young but gifted priestess they send on errands when one needs to be placated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, something to point out because i forgot before, relationships can go either way. All of the kinds of beings that might generate allies, friends or lovers could be in different circunstances the source of enemies or rivals. And one can always mix up things for fun and surprises, like one of the resistance's lieutenants - and the abyssal's paramour - being the god's half-human child, the god of caravans being the god of the mountain's rival not only for influence but the interests of a certain oasis' goddess and so on. mxing and matching parts can be quite good for novelty.<br /> <br /> Like making a manticore trader, because that's what the dying mortal consumed to generate it was (just replaced the &quot;Consumed Knowledge&quot; 5 dice pool of the Manticore with the Assess Goods, Read Motive &amp; Social Influence pools [6-7 dice] of the Snakefolk Merchant QC) for an example. I do these kinds of tweaks &amp; reskins from NPCs in the core all the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 So far the resistance has been targetting the mine to weaken the Realm influence - but a potential wealth that comes from it could be used as an incentive to get some nobles on their side. That's how revolutions are financed, whatever simple people would like to think. (Also, while mistreatment of slaves is obviously a thing, as are various horrors of Exalted, I don't want to make my campaign too dark. My player and I used to have a World of Darkness storyteller who used to overdo it, and the campaign crashed and burned from darkness-induced audience apathy.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand wanting to keep the grimdark at bay for the sake of adventure and fun. Truth be told, my &quot;lord of the pit&quot; alternate take of the god in itself wasn't meant to be (much) darker than your average Storm Mother - i did imagine the god <i>giving occasional help and making deals with the slaves too, playing both sides to his benefit</i>, in fact - though i can see how the parts about buried beings under the sand of millenia might give that pitchblack world feel. Spur of moment writing, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Speaking of supernaturally-powered people stealing stuff to finance revolutions, try to watch Ninja Scroll. It's a classic reference for Exalted inspiration, to boot. And while a completely different setting in too many ludricous ways, maybe Code Geass too.<br /> <br /> Also, for a little twist, what if the resistance was using tunnels in the mines as hideouts for their gear and personnel - maybe also liberating angry/vengeful slaves to join the revolution? How does that side for a deathknight throwing a little curveball?<br /> <br /> And before i forget, how about a groundhog lunar wandering beneath the earth, or a young blind earth aspected outcaste that moves about with a pack of elemental tunnel burrowing giant moles? <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burrow\" target=\"_blank\">Also</a>, possibly of interest on ideas on visuals for lunar, elemental or fae critters below the earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6 So, the resistance would stoop to grave-robbing to produce evil spirits that could be chained to their service? An interesting idea. How can a mortal enslave a hungry ghost without getting his throat torn out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely doable, though i can't remember specific mechanics as such or pages. The core and other books might have stuff to help along with zombie-related occult fluff i believe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 The sidereal is pushing his own agenda, but not really scheming against Ragara so far - if only because their presence there offers the city more stability than the current alternative. So he actually does help them foil the more sinister moves against them. As for the Dragon blooded, turning against the Realm hasn't crossed their minds just yet, although the younger ones definitely resent being stuck without support on what they consider a backwater. That also means they'd try to kill the PC if they discovered her now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving a quick perusal of the officers in your notes. My first thoughts are:<br /> Ragara Salabus - Experienced Dragon-Blood QC.<br /> <br /> Ragara Salta - Not half the schemer he thinks he is, if he can't brew schemes of his own away from court.<br /> <br /> Possibly a prime mark for a real schemer to exploit. That said, probably the person to keep a correspondence with relatives or associates in the capital going.<br /> <br /> Ragara Davero - Poor guy, has exactly the traits to fail horribly at wooing Kalga. I ask myself how would he react to someone succeding (while he recovers from the wounds of the cliff drop)....<br /> <br /> Captain Virmo - Being a soldier is hazardous enough on itself, but getting himself in a position where he's the lone mortal in the table of demigods, is the guy suicidal? Either that or Dragonlord Salabus REALLY likes and trusts him (lover, bastard child, old friend or son of an old friend, etc?).<br /> <br /> Ragara Verda - also probably a quite decent tracker and the first to appear if the people start screaming &quot;monster&quot; or &quot;anathema!&quot;, no doubt.<br /> <br /> Ragara Dereks - Young Dynast QC meets spoiled brat (damn shame Irin's overdose plan botched. kind of expected, but still).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8 I don't think the quicksand quite fits, but he could definitely have a darker side. Even in real life mythology, mine gods and spirits are usually fickle, even if benevolent. After all, they also embody the OSHA rules of the mine - disrespecting those can get you killed really quickly. So far I'm imagining him as a kind of spoiled aristocrat stereotype - too vain and greedy to realise how dangerously stupid he is (kind of like the badger god in the old Sidereal book introductory comic. ) EDIT: I checked notes, and the mountain is a dead volcano. So your plan could work - although the god probably has no authority or enough power to make the mountain erupt again without some Yu Shan paperwork. Definitely a direction to explore in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so he is a mountain (dromant volcano) god - there goes my &quot;god of the pit/quicksand&quot; version to homebrew limbo. As an aside, i was under the impression strip mines are done in level ground areas instead of hills or mountains, guess i'm wrong, mistakes from quick-glance research. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Definitely changes some things. That said, stealing tricks from the Storm Mother to adapt to an earth theme - avalanche or landslides instead of waves &amp; storms, firedust or lava in place of lightning, is perfectly doable and a great way to give a surprising hard edge under all the spoiled fatcat softness. It also brings up some other <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volcanic_rock#Mineralogy\" target=\"_blank\">bounty</a> possibilities for him to offer enterprising individuals. Not to mention you now have the extra option of tunnels/lava tubes to play labyrinthine spelunking/dungeoncrawl with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1404831#post1404831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want more details, here are my campaign notes so far (there is some captain obvious info there - it was meant for brainstorming with people unfamiliar with Exalted)<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Vots16qiWe9az3Gea8XjybufAf2tCEvjYrrWC5rODBk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...rWC5rODBk/edit</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Checking it and added some comments above accordingly. Lots of misadventures i see....<br /> <br /> Hope you have fun with the input and suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-30-2020, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T18:36:37-07:00","id":1405443,"title":"","content":"Others have spoken of the possibility of Kirimu the generous, the god of the mountain &amp; mine, making deals or browbeating earth elementals into working for him and i agree that bringing elementals into the mix could bring a number of hooks and options to the table.<br /> <br /> Braninthejar, you have 2e books, no? One thing that might be of inestimable utility and inspiration in devising themes for elementals and their powers would be the &quot;associations&quot; box in page 48 of the Oadenol's codex, that explores the subject of how elemental (and celestial) aspects may express themselves and the points of thematic intercession/overlap that may exist between them.<br /> <br /> If you don't have it, the section on the supernatural qualities and resonances of the many types of jade in Arms of Chosen can certainly serve to fill the same thematic inspiration role in coming up with your own weirdly colored alien people, beasts &amp; such, i guess.<br /> <br /> With that &quot;dirty mechanics&quot; part out of the way, i would like to speak a bit on their narrative options, fluff &amp; possible roles in the current lore. While not word by word, some bits straight from the 3e corebook:<br /> (These focus more to elementals of &quot;natural&quot; origin - those shaped by a sorcerer's will may have some themes uniquely their own, but that is for another post)<br /> <br /> - Elementals are <b>not</b> divine representatives or overseers of places, things, or concepts. No portfolio and cosmic role do they fill and any duties or responsibilities are completely self-imposed, by virtue of either choice or coercion, force &amp; manipulation. But beholden to or defined by such things they are not.<br /> <br /> - <b>No </b>spirit-sanctums and temples in (or outside of) Creation await them, except those taken by virtue of either force, guile or luck and even then it is a given/taken abode of a glorified tenant (or squatter).<br /> <br /> - The elemental races are old beyond measure. Before men, before beasts, and some say before even the gods, elementals have stalked Creation, birthed into the world from the interplay of the world\u2019s natural energies. Storm fronts, forest fires, earthquakes, mudslides, deep ocean currents, lightning strikes and blizzards, the heat-haze of the desert and the crushing force of the avalanche are their careless unresponsive deadbeat parents of sorts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The last fragment in particular<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">, the idea of elemental races going side by side with primordial races, playing out as either allies, enemies, rivals and/or surrogates to Dragon Kings, Jadeborn, Lintha and a number of the strange beings inhabiting still in the shores of the Dreaming Sea, is a major change from elemental portrayal in previous editions and a most welcome one, at least imho.</span> </div> </div> </div>- Being products of the (super)natural cycles of Creation, elementals are beings of the <b>material world</b>, closer to fauna, flora and mortals in perspective and experience than the numinous beings of Yu-shan, Underworld, Malfeas and stranger abodes. Caverns, cities, clouds, deserts, forests, mountains, palaces, plains, ravines, rivers, seas are some of the many other demesnes and places, enchanted or mundane, may they be found on and in some cases decide to call home.<br /> <br /> - Plant, beast, person, monster, hero, devil, god: any or all of those things they may be, alternately or at the same time, depending on their interactions with the physical world around them and whatever crosses their path and leaves a mark upon them, for good or for ill. In that they can be peculiarly strange in many ways and yet curiously similar to the recently Exalted trying to find a place in Creation for themselves and their barely understood powers and urges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, i wouldn't be surprised if the first exposure of many (individual) elementals to the idea of themselves as divine or at least supernatural was through the perspective, first contacts and interaction with mortals, what in itself may bring an interesting twist and angles to their variegated stories.<br /> <br /> And now i'm imagining some people dedicated to seeking out freshly spawned elementals of certain sorts to manipulate into becoming the gods, demigods and heroes of their city-state or nation. Or a sorcerer maintaining a &quot;provider of gods&quot; scam through elemental &amp;/or demon summoning and lots of chicanery. </div> </div> </div>Anyway, my point was that elementals in 3e can be far closer to wyld mutants, non-human races or exalts than gods &amp; demons per se and consequently may have as mundane desires or needs, though with an alien/weird spin. They might have a desire for things they see as exotic, pleasant &amp; valuable and cunning mortals (or a self-serving god guiding them) take advantage of this through commerce or the exchange of favors and services.<br /> <br /> Oh, just remembered some earth elementals <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QEuUgNRGcEs\" target=\"_blank\">have teeth made of precious stones</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, little but relevant aside. Not all &quot;natural born&quot; elementals have to be part of inhuman races or exotic beasts/monsters. In fact, <a href=\"https://www.livefertile.com/blog/food-fertility-and-folklore-cabbage\" target=\"_blank\">some</a> elementals could be very much part of human societies, even be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momotar%C5%8D#Story\" target=\"_blank\">quite popular figures</a> among &quot;their&quot; respective people instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-30-2020, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-31T17:09:02-07:00","id":1405698,"title":"","content":"Off to a short vacation. Will think on all this and write when I'm back<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T17:04:24-07:00","id":1406526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1405220#post1405220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Checking it and added some comments above accordingly. Lots of misadventures i see....<br /> <br /> Hope you have fun with the input and suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did some thinking while away from work (turns out swimming works best for me for tuning stuff out and coming up with ideas) The answers and suggestions coalesced into a story arc in my mind and now I have something I can work with.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's just a sketch at the moment. I can still benefit from advice (coming up with details, minor complications, villain mistakes that could make for interesting investigation rolls, and generally turning the synopsis into actual adventures. )<br /> <br /> So far the idea looks like this:<br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- While trying to expand their fields towards the slope, some farmers dig up human bones. It turns out there is quite a lot of stuff buried there under old volcanic ash. After examining the situation, the dracon realises there is some old settlement there, buried long ago by an eruption, and forbids people from digging there for fear of accidentally hitting a buried shadowland.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- A couple people get brutally killed in town. Hungry ghosts are to blame. Shadow Spindle, a foreign exorcist who has just arrived with a caravan, offers to handle the ghosts. Meanwhile, an investigation reveals that someone has defiled a number of fresh graves, causing the monsters to raise. A small cell of cultists is discovered and wiped out, but sergeant Jabbar is killed in the fight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Kirimu asks the PC to appeal to the priests, to make him the patron god of the city. He knows this is a controversial demand, but he has faith in her ability of persuasion, and he\u2019s willing to pay (with some treasures from the buried settlement - but he won\u2019t reveal that, or why the settlement had been destroyed to begin with.) As it turns out, there is a formal problem, as the city actually does have a god, though people barely remember him. Shimobaba, the old camel-headed god used to control the wells the settlement had sprung up around. But when the aqueduct was built, he found himself suddenly losing influence - the village grew into a city, but no longer really needed him, and between the gods of trade and travel blessing the caravans, and Kirimu controlling the other biggest source of income, he fell into obscurity, only receiving his due prayers thanks to the immaculate monks that moved in some time after.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- The dracon sends Dereks out of town to hunt some rebels, and to get him out of public sight for a while. While he has some success, confirming that the rebels are using old tombs in the mountains as hideouts, and even takes some captives, he also indulges in petty cruelty towards locals who might be helping rebels, and as soon as he comes back, he begins some \u2018investigation\u2019 in town, causing problems to merchants that had agreed to finance the PCs pet project, under the guise of fulfilling the dracon\u2019s orders.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- The mayor\u2019s son is coming of age, and a big party is announced. A couple days before the event, the ghost of sergeant Jabbar appears to the PC, begging her to help his teenage daughter against some unspecified threat. As it turns out, the girl dreamed of attending the party, something way above her station. Turns out something listened, and decided to \u2018help\u2019, and now both her and the mayor\u2019s son are being slowly brainwashed into reenacting a twisted version of Cinderella. If the raksha isn\u2019t found and stopped, a lot of people will suffer. (and if she is thwarted but survives, she\u2019ll gladly go for an epic revenge story instead.)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- A plague hits the city. The PC will want to save as many patients as possible, while keeping her powers secret, and looking for the source. It turns out the aqueduct has been tampered with, poisoning the city with tainted water. As people are warned to use the wells instead, some voices blame Shimobaba for the ordeal - after all the god of the wells seems to be the only one to profit from the disaster. (The accusations are sponsored by Kirimu, who bribed some of the locals to cast blame upon his rival)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soon after, the Realm army announces that they found a man responsible for the sabotage, and are going to execute him. During the execution, he frees himself from the gag, and shouts some dire threats, in the process incriminating the rebels before being killed. (in truth, he was one of the rebels captured much earlier during Dereks\u2019 investigation. Captain Salta broke him with torture and talked him into betraying his cause in return for a relatively quick death as well as sparing his family - he figured that since the desert dwellers have a big taboo against tampering with water, he can use trickery to galvanize the locals against the rebel forces). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- The ghost of Jabbar visits the PC again, delivering another warning - the dead don\u2019t rest easy. This is the true reason for the plague - the cultists poisoned the aqueduct while Shadow Spindle, their necromancer mastermind used his sorcerous working to defile the place where the plague victims were to be buried, returning every night to enslave the hungry ghosts as they arose. Right now he is almost ready to unleash them on the city in a night of slaughter. <br /> <br /> Some more details on the player:<br /> 1 She is an ex-nurse, and enjoys medical mysteries, even minor ones, such as when a merchant had a sudden diaharrea and feared poison, but it turned out he had tried to improve his 'performance' for a younger wife, and someone sold him rheum instead of ginsang. (works better in Polish, where that makes a pun)<br /> 2 She hates dungeon runs. Fighting the enemy in his lair is stupid, and through the years I've seen her flood a dungeon, send lava worms through load-bearing walls, or even abandon some plot threads altogether rather than deal with sentries and traps. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T05:20:43-07:00","id":1406745,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the long wait, yesterday i was a little dispersed, but here goes some attempt at input &amp; suggestions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- While trying to expand their fields towards the slope, some farmers dig up human bones. It turns out there is quite a lot of stuff buried there under old volcanic ash. After examining the situation, the dracon realises there is some old settlement there, buried long ago by an eruption, and forbids people from digging there for fear of accidentally hitting a buried shadowland.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- A couple people get brutally killed in town. Hungry ghosts are to blame. Shadow Spindle, a foreign exorcist who has just arrived with a caravan, offers to handle the ghosts. Meanwhile, an investigation reveals that someone has defiled a number of fresh graves, causing the monsters to raise. A small cell of cultists is discovered and wiped out, but sergeant Jabbar is killed in the fight.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Rumors - false or true - about the old settlement's size and quantity of buried lost riches could lead curious/greedy people to try to dig in the area, before or after the dragon-blooded commander orders the area cordoned off. Some people might or not claim the hungry ghosts come from desecrating that old, recently discovered place, what might complicate the investigation (is it a red herring, the defiled fresh graves are or <b>both </b>serve as sources of desecrated undead?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Kirimu asks the PC to appeal to the priests, to make him the patron god of the city. He knows this is a controversial demand, but he has faith in her ability of persuasion, and he\u2019s willing to pay (with some treasures from the buried settlement - but he won\u2019t reveal that, or why the settlement had been destroyed to begin with.) As it turns out, there is a formal problem, as the city actually does have a god, though people barely remember him. Shimobaba, the old camel-headed god used to control the wells the settlement had sprung up around. But when the aqueduct was built, he found himself suddenly losing influence - the village grew into a city, but no longer really needed him, and between the gods of trade and travel blessing the caravans, and Kirimu controlling the other biggest source of income, he fell into obscurity, only receiving his due prayers thanks to the immaculate monks that moved in some time after.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it could be that the old god is the rare one that cares more about doing its duty - in particular, taking care of the wells - than gathering influence and worship from mortals. Not to mention, think of the long game. Riches come and go, cities may rise or be abandoned, engineering works require maintenance, but water will be valuable for people and animals no matter what.<br /> That kind of relaxed &amp; patient attitude in itself could make <span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shimobaba </span></span>an interesting figure for contrast with Kirimu, the caravan gods and other ambitious, politicking types. Also, as his purview is the old wells as much as the city, he would definitely have a considerable dislike of the Deathknight and his agents shenanigans.<br /> <br /> (At least until some cultist offers to explode one of the aqueduct's pillars with stolen firedust, in exchange for the city god's help in facilitating the revolutionaries navigation/hiding through the city's streets - and sabotaging/misdirecting any pursuing enemies - that is)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- The dracon sends Dereks out of town to hunt some rebels, and to get him out of public sight for a while. While he has some success, confirming that the rebels are using old tombs in the mountains as hideouts, and even takes some captives, he also indulges in petty cruelty towards locals who might be helping rebels, and as soon as he comes back, he begins some \u2018investigation\u2019 in town, causing problems to merchants that had agreed to finance the PCs pet project, under the guise of fulfilling the dracon\u2019s orders.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What if some merchants or common workers from families hurt by Dereks' &quot;law enforcing works&quot; start to discuss ways of thwarting him, if not outright assassination attempts? The cultists could definitely exploit this to gain more followers, allies and contacts, even if they decide not to directly against him (as killing Dereks might get the Realm forces to clamp down even harder on the local people depending on how it is done).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- The mayor\u2019s son is coming of age, and a big party is announced. A couple days before the event, the ghost of sergeant Jabbar appears to the PC, begging her to help his teenage daughter against some unspecified threat. As it turns out, the girl dreamed of attending the party, something way above her station. Turns out something listened, and decided to \u2018help\u2019, and now both her and the mayor\u2019s son are being slowly brainwashed into reenacting a twisted version of Cinderella. If the raksha isn\u2019t found and stopped, a lot of people will suffer. (and if she is thwarted but survives, she\u2019ll gladly go for an epic revenge story instead.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Mayor? How about a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheikh\" target=\"_blank\">sheikh</a> instead, for some <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_EVlNhmTEPI\" target=\"_blank\">Aladdin</a> on your Cinderella tale?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now i'm imagining a twisted version of the genie's lamp - basically a non-weaponized Asphodel (from Arms of Chosen) stocked with the souls/dreams of previous successful users and whoever they conquered/defeated/seduced through their (short) lives. Wishes from the genie/fae godmother as spells (or chimerical equivalents).<br /> <br /> Don't know if it helps anything, but had to blurt that stuff out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- A plague hits the city. The PC will want to save as many patients as possible, while keeping her powers secret, and looking for the source. It turns out the aqueduct has been tampered with, poisoning the city with tainted water. As people are warned to use the wells instead, some voices blame Shimobaba for the ordeal - after all the god of the wells seems to be the only one to profit from the disaster. (The accusations are sponsored by Kirimu, who bribed some of the locals to cast blame upon his rival)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The great question is - who really did it? The cultists (after a deal with Shimobaba or on their own), Kirimu, some 3rd party (like a corrupt merchant that has access to water sources from outside the city looking to make himself rich from the distrust climate) acting for mysterious reasons its own?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soon after, the Realm army announces that they found a man responsible for the sabotage, and are going to execute him. During the execution, he frees himself from the gag, and shouts some dire threats, in the process incriminating the rebels before being killed. (in truth, he was one of the rebels captured much earlier during Dereks\u2019 investigation. Captain Salta broke him with torture and talked him into betraying his cause in return for a relatively quick death as well as sparing his family - he figured that since the desert dwellers have a big taboo against tampering with water, he can use trickery to galvanize the locals against the rebel forces).</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what if some people - who are quite aware of dragon-blooded cruelty through Derek's petty sadism - point out that it might all be a lie? If someone comes up with evidence (true or false) of disonesty of the dead rebel's confession, it could lead into people turning against the local Ragara forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- The ghost of Jabbar visits the PC again, delivering another warning - the dead don\u2019t rest easy. This is the true reason for the plague - the cultists poisoned the aqueduct while Shadow Spindle, their necromancer mastermind used his sorcerous working to defile the place where the plague victims were to be buried, returning every night to enslave the hungry ghosts as they arose. Right now he is almost ready to unleash them on the city in a night of slaughter.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Jabbar seems quite active and well-informed - does the dead officer have allies of his own in opposing the cultists' evil works? Or could it be a front from another ghost passing for him?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1402484-what-would-your-god-do?p=1406526#post1406526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#050505\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some more details on the player:<br /> 1 She is an ex-nurse, and enjoys medical mysteries, even minor ones, such as when a merchant had a sudden diaharrea and feared poison, but it turned out he had tried to improve his 'performance' for a younger wife, and someone sold him rheum instead of ginsang. (works better in Polish, where that makes a pun)<br /> 2 She hates dungeon runs. Fighting the enemy in his lair is stupid, and through the years I've seen her flood a dungeon, send lava worms through load-bearing walls, or even abandon some plot threads altogether rather than deal with sentries and traps. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, getting the occasional episode of House, the Good Doctor and some other medical dramas - with some period adaptations - should provide you with plenty of fodder to throw her way and she to toy with i guess.<br /> <br /> Also, not every ruin has to be a boss lair style dungeon, to be dealt with by fighting every little step of the way. Think of it as archeological digs - real ones of cinematographic - with some fantastic twists in the form of ghosts, spirits, artifacts or hearthstones and other stuff.<br /> <br /> And for something of a twist - what if for once the player is the one that gets a chance to make a secret lair of her own from an empty, buried <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaymakli_Underground_City\" target=\"_blank\">but far from ruined city</a>? As long as she can put to rest any lingering ghosts) or elemental squatters, ancient &amp; medieval people had <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Book_of_Healing#Earth_sciences\" target=\"_blank\">interesting ideas about natural processes</a> that might offer ideas on geomancy or creatures) could be a perfect place for making a large underground (duh!) clinic, guerilla hideouts, smuggler's plaza and much more besides. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Speaking of settlements taken by volcanoes, <a href=\"https://allthatsinteresting.com/bodies-of-pompeii\" target=\"_blank\">an ur example</a>, with a little something that could lead to something between ghost &amp; elemental, strange cast-effigies of sorts (an alternate explanation for walking statue antagonists?).<br /> <br /> Damn, i can even imagine some bold people with a little occult knowledge striking some form of deal with any lingering ghosts - &quot;you let us stay, locals will occasionally pray and make some offerings for the dead&quot; - Pretty sweet deal for any ghosts without descendants to care for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-07-2020, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}